3. **The baseline gap (36.41 vs reference 30.8) warrants investigation**—implementation details may matter more than the learning mechanism.

4. **Contrastive learning's value depends on target complexity**: Periodicity invariance (PerioGT) benefits from contrastive learning because it's not directly computable. Rigidity does not benefit because it IS computable.

