ALL current approaches predict Tg as a **static function of structure**, but glass transition is fundamentally **kinetic** - it depends on cooling rate, thermal history, and cooperative segment dynamics. This is the fundamental mismatch.

**Conceptual Leap Sources:**
1. **Adam-Gibbs theory**: Tg relates to cooperatively rearranging regions (CRRs) whose size ξ(T) grows as T→Tg, analogous to correlation length in critical phenomena
