```
Proposed: Universal thermodynamic laws (Tg<Tm, Tg/Tm ratio) do NOT provide sufficient 
supervision signal for learning useful representations.

Evidence: TCP pre-training achieved 100% thermodynamic consistency but showed 0% improvement 
in Tg prediction (35.49 vs 35.22 K scratch). Physics constraints are too weak to guide 
representation learning.

Implication: Physics-informed approaches should focus on feature engineering (Day 2, Day 5) 
and loss functions (Day 6), NOT pre-training objectives.
```

